### 2d. Tier 5 codes mirrored from DistQLDPC (2026-10-23)

24 tier5 stems that previously shipped only in DistQLDPC were copied unchanged (same
matrices and stems as DistQLDPC main e52d15b): the LP_* and TN_* stems listed in 2a,
plus the following.

- BB_756_16_30to34, BB_864_4_30to40, BB_1080_4_30to48: GPL-3.0-or-later (as 2b).
  Lower bound 30 from DistQLDPC's optional connected-cluster engine (GH-133/GH-138).
  Upper bounds come from GF(2)-verified logical operators found by DistQLDPC's GH-146
  finder, as do the upper bounds of the TN_*_{lb}to{ub} stems.
- LP_1122_148_20 and LP_2610_744_16: the lifted-product codes lp20^{3,5} [[1122,148]]
  and lp16^{3,7} [[2610,744]] of M. Cain et al., arXiv:2603.28627 (2026), Appendix A.1,
  Eqs. (A3) and (A5). The matrices were built by DistQLDPC from the seed matrices listed
  in C. Crocker's Zenodo record (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23379787, v1.1
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23445463, CC BY 4.0), which first established d = 20 and d = 16.
  DistQLDPC re-verified both values.
- C. Crocker's record also published d = 20 for [[1054,140]] (LP_1054_140_20) before
  DistQLDPC, and it independently agrees with d = 16 for LP_714_100_16 and LP_1020_136_16.

For the canonical attribution text and dated rename notes, see DistQLDPC
[NOTICE](https://github.com/guluchen/DistQLDPC/blob/main/NOTICE) and
data/matrices/README.md.

